      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested — Please split this CL**\n\n### Review Summary\n\n* **Functionality:**\n  * **`timeout_ms \u003d\u003d 0` Boundary Bug (`util/rts5817_usb_device.cc`, line 56):** `wait_for_device()` checks `if (timeout_ms \u003c 0 || poll_interval_ms \u003c\u003d 0)`, which allows `timeout_ms \u003d\u003d 0` through. Because the polling loop condition is `for (int waited \u003d 0; waited \u003c timeout_ms; ...)`, passing `timeout_ms \u003d\u003d 0` still releases existing resources and calls `backend_-\u003einit()`, executes zero `open()` attempts, and immediately fails. Check `timeout_ms \u003c\u003d 0` up front.\n  * **Device Handle Leak on Repeated `open()` (`util/rts5817_libusb_backend.cc`, lines 19–26):** Unlike `RtsLibusbBackend::init()`, `RtsLibusbBackend::open()` overwrites `dev_handle_` without closing an already-open handle if called again before `close()`.\n  * **Uncompiled Source Files (`util/build.mk`, lines 50–61):** `util/rts5817_libusb_backend.h` and `util/rts5817_libusb_backend.cc` are added in this CL, but `util/build.mk` only compiles `rts5817_usb_device.o` and `rts5817_usb_device_test.o`, leaving `rts5817_libusb_backend.{h,cc}` uncompiled by `make BOARD\u003dhost utils-test` and `make BOARD\u003dhost utils-host`.\n* **Architecture \u0026 Component Fit:**\n  * Introducing `RtsUsbBackend` and `MockRtsUsbBackend` cleanly decouples `RtsUsbDevice` from physical `libusb` hardware and aligns well with sibling host utilities in `util/` (such as `util/elan`). However, `RtsLibusbBackend` should be introduced in the CL that wires `rts5817_libusb_backend.o` into `util/build.mk` so it is compiled in the commit that adds it.\n* **Code Simplicity:**\n  * The control flow in `RtsUsbDevice::init()`, `wait_for_device()`, `release()`, and `enable_download()` is concise and direct, with injectable `SleepFn` avoiding real-time sleeps in unit tests.\n* **Idiomaticity \u0026 Readability:**\n  * **Header Constants (`util/rts5817