 130), **13 lines of build rules** (`util/build.mk`), and **234 lines of test/mock code** (`rts5817_mock_usb_backend.h`: 27, `rts5817_usb_device_test.cc`: 207). Because the non-test production diff exceeds the 250-line limit (`343 \u003e\u003d 250`) and bundles three distinct logical components (`RtsUsbDevice` lifecycle, RTS5817 vendor download-mode control, and an uncompiled `RtsLibusbBackend`), please split this CL:\n    1. **CL 1:** Add `RtsUsbBackend` (`init`, `open`, `close`, `error_name`), `MockRtsUsbBackend`, `RtsUsbDevice` lifecycle management (`init`, `wait_for_device`, `release`), lifecycle unit tests in `util/rts5817_usb_device_test.cc`, and `util/build.mk` (~185 non-test lines).\n    2. **CL 2:** Add `is_open()` and `control_transfer()` to `RtsUsbBackend`/`MockRtsUsbBackend`, RTS5817 vendor download-mode control (`enable_download()` and request constants), and the `EnableDownload*` unit tests (~75 non-test lines).\n    3. **CL 3:** Add `RtsLibusbBackend` (`util/rts5817_libusb_backend.h` and `util/rts5817_libusb_backend.cc`, ~94 lines) and wire `rts5817_libusb_backend.o` into `util/build.mk` (or fold it into the `rts5817_flash` CLI CL where `rts5817_libusb_backend.o` is linked).\n* **Commit Message:**\n  * Avoid joining multiple responsibilities with `\" and \"` in the subject line and remove the patch-series staging narration in the third paragraph. See the inline comment on `/COMMIT_MSG` for copy-pasteable commit messages.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/594e9a3e-3b69-40fd-bca9-90bbce87b9e8)",
