      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Prevent Handle Leak If `open()` Is Called While Already Open:**\n\nUnlike `init()` (which calls `close()` before re-initializing `ctx_`), calling `open()` when `dev_handle_` is already non-null overwrites `dev_handle_` without calling `libusb_close(dev_handle_)`, leaking the existing device handle. Close any existing `dev_handle_` before opening a new one:\n\n```cpp\nbool RtsLibusbBackend::open(uint16_t vid, uint16_t pid)\n{\n\tif (!ctx_)\n\t\treturn false;\n\n\tif (dev_handle_) {\n\t\tlibusb_close(dev_handle_);\n\t\tdev_handle_ \u003d nullptr;\n\t}\n\n\tdev_handle_ \u003d libusb_open_device_with_vid_pid(ctx_, vid, pid);\n\treturn dev_handle_ !\u003d nullptr;\n}\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/594e9a3e-3b69-40fd-bca9-90bbce87b9e8)",
