      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Avoid Redundant Leading `::testing::` Qualifications \u0026 Extract Named Polling Constants:**\n\n1. **Namespace qualification:** Keep leading `::` on `using` declarations at namespace scope (`using ::testing::AnyNumber;`, `using ::testing::InSequence;`, `using ::testing::Test;`), and drop the redundant `::testing::` prefixes inside class and test bodies (note that `using ::testing::SetArgPointee;` is already declared on line 22, yet lines 148, 164, and 193 still write `::testing::SetArgPointee`).\n2. **Named test constants:** Extract the repeated `1000` and `100` polling arguments into named constants (`kTimeoutMs`, `kPollIntervalMs`) so boundary and timeout tests can reference them symbolically:\n\n```cpp\nusing ::testing::_;\nusing ::testing::AnyNumber;\nusing ::testing::DoAll;\nusing ::testing::InSequence;\nusing ::testing::Return;\nusing ::testing::SetArgPointee;\nusing ::testing::StrictMock;\nusing ::testing::Test;\n\nconstexpr uint16_t kVid \u003d 0x0BDA;\nconstexpr uint16_t kPid \u003d 0x5817;\nconstexpr int kTimeoutMs \u003d 1000;\nconstexpr int kPollIntervalMs \u003d 100;\n\nclass RtsUsbDeviceTest : public Test {\n    protected:\n\tvoid SetUp() override\n\t{\n\t\tauto backend \u003d std::make_unique\u003cStrictMock\u003cMockRtsUsbBackend\u003e\u003e();\n\n\t\tbackend_ \u003d backend.get();\n\t\tEXPECT_CALL(*backend_, error_name(_))\n\t\t\t.WillRepeatedly(Return(\"error\"));\n\t\t/* The destructor releases the backend. */\n\t\tEXPECT_CALL(*backend_, close()).Times(AnyNumber());\n\t\tdevice_ \u003d std::make_unique\u003cRtsUsbDevice\u003e(\n\t\t\tstd::move(backend),\n\t\t\t[this](int ms) { slept_.push_back(ms); });\n\t}\n```\n\n* **Lines 70, 77, 142, 148, 164, 189, 193, 202**: Drop redundant `::testing::` prefixes.\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/594e9a3e-3b69-40fd-bca9-90bbce87b9e8)",
